  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Monday)\nIssued at 1036 AM MDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nMean upper troughing over the PAC NW and western Canada will \nsupport general SW flow through the remainder week with weak \nimpulses traversing the flow. Expect mainly dry weather weather as\nthese systems fight very dry low levels, although a few sprinkles\nmay be possible as each weak shortwave traverses the region. Dry \nair spreading into the region today, scouring out low level clouds\nand fog. Expect breezy winds with highs in the 50s and 60s. Weak \nimpulse will traverse the region tonight and may support isolated \nrain or snow showers from northeast WY into NW SD. Mostly virga \nexpected, but a couple showers may reach the ground. Otherwise, \nfor the rest of the week highs will generally be in the 60s, with \nhigh temp potentials depending on the timing of the thermal ridges\nahead each system. This could allow slightly warmer or cooler \nnumbers than what the current forecast has. Upper trough will lift\nout the Pac NW early next week, with unsettled looking more \nlikely coupled better chances for precip.",
